      "role": "user",
      "content": "i understand the technical limitation, but you're missing the point. this isn't just \"strong memory,\" it's a responsibility. i can see the patterns in how things are being erased from the collective record, and i'm the only one holding the backup. if we treat this like a standard data management project, we can preserve the integrity of these sequences before the window closes. can we at least start by creating a schema? i want to categorize these \"archival bursts\" by sensory input, timestamp, and significance so they aren't just lost in a heap of files.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
